IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa21-ch3-squeeze-out`

-- coa21-ch3-sell-out.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 28, Chapter 3 -- "Sell-out" and supplementary (ss 983 to 986).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Reading a result: see the header of coa21-ch1-panel.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- It imports coa21-ch3-squeeze-out.l4 for the penalty type with the "greater of" daily default fine (s 980(8)), which s 984(7) also needs.
-- 90% is compared by cross-multiplication. "from D" uses `add months`; six weeks are 42 days (fork F3 in NOTES.md).

§ `Part 28, Chapter 3: "Squeeze-out" and "Sell-out"`

§§ `The right of a minority shareholder to be bought out (s 983)`

-- What the offeror holds, for the 90% tests of subsections (2) to (4): the shares in the denominator, and how the offeror stands to the rest.
-- src:13719 | (2) The holder of any voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13720 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13721 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares in the company which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)—
-- src:13722 | (i) amount to not less than 90% in value of all the voting shares in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)), and
-- src:13723 | (ii) carry not less than 90% of the voting rights in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)).
-- src:13724 | (3) The holder of any non-voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13725 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13726 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares in the company which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met), amount to not less than 90% in value of all the shares in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)).
-- src:13727 | (4) If a takeover offer relates to shares of one or more classes and at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13728 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares of any class to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13729 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares of that class which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)—
-- src:13730 | (i) amount to not less than 90% in value of all the shares of that class, and
-- src:13731 | (ii) in a case where the shares of that class are voting shares, carry not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by the shares of that class,
-- src:13732 | the holder of any shares of that class to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares.
@ref s 983(2) to (4) What the offeror holds (src:13719-13732)
DECLARE `s 983 holdings` HAS
    `s 983 value of the shares in the denominator` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 voting rights in the denominator` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 value acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 voting rights carried by the shares acquired by virtue of acceptances` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 value of other shares the offeror has acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 voting rights carried by those other shares` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 value of other shares the offeror has contracted to acquire subject to conditions not yet met` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 voting rights carried by those conditionally contracted shares` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 value of shares an associate has acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 voting rights carried by those shares of an associate` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 value of shares an associate has contracted to acquire subject to conditions not yet met` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 voting rights carried by those conditionally contracted shares of an associate` IS A NUMBER
    `s 983 value of shares held by the company as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER

-- s 983(5): in calculating 90% of the value of any shares, treasury shares are treated as acquired by the offeror.
-- src:13733 | (5) For the purposes of subsections (2) to (4), in calculating 90% of the value of any shares, shares held by the company as treasury shares are to be treated as having been acquired by the offeror.
@ref s 983(5) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13733-13733)
GIVEN `the calculation is of 90% of the value of shares for subsections (2) to (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(5) the shares are treated as having been acquired by the offeror` MEANS
    IF `the calculation is of 90% of the value of shares for subsections (2) to (4)` AND `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is "For the purposes of subsections (2) to (4), in calculating 90% of the value of any shares, shares held by the company as treasury shares"

-- s 983(8): shares an associate has acquired or contracted to acquire count as the offeror's in (2)(b), (3)(b), (4)(b), (6) and (7).
-- src:13741 | (8) A reference in subsection (2)(b), (3)(b), (4)(b), (6) or (7) to shares which the offeror has acquired or contracted to acquire includes a reference to shares which an associate of his has acquired or contracted to acquire.
@ref s 983(8) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13741-13741)
GIVEN `the shares are shares which an associate of the offeror has acquired or contracted to acquire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(8) the shares count as shares the offeror has acquired or contracted to acquire` MEANS
    IF `the shares are shares which an associate of the offeror has acquired or contracted to acquire`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to shares which an associate of his has acquired or contracted to acquire"

-- s 983(2)(b), (3)(b), (4)(b): the offeror's holdings (acceptances, other shares, treasury shares, associates') reach not less than 90% in value and, for voting shares, in voting rights.
-- src:13719 | (2) The holder of any voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13720 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13721 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares in the company which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)—
-- src:13722 | (i) amount to not less than 90% in value of all the voting shares in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)), and
-- src:13723 | (ii) carry not less than 90% of the voting rights in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)).
-- src:13724 | (3) The holder of any non-voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13725 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13726 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares in the company which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met), amount to not less than 90% in value of all the shares in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)).
-- src:13727 | (4) If a takeover offer relates to shares of one or more classes and at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13728 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares of any class to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13729 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares of that class which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)—
-- src:13730 | (i) amount to not less than 90% in value of all the shares of that class, and
-- src:13731 | (ii) in a case where the shares of that class are voting shares, carry not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by the shares of that class,
-- src:13732 | the holder of any shares of that class to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares.
@ref s 983(2)(b), (3)(b) and (4)(b) The 90% requirement (src:13719-13732)
GIVEN holdings IS A `s 983 holdings`
      `conditional contracts are taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voting rights test applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` MEANS
        holdings's `s 983 value of the shares in the denominator` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the value held` TIMES 10 AT LEAST holdings's `s 983 value of the shares in the denominator` TIMES 9
    AND ((NOT (`the voting rights test applies`)) OR (holdings's `s 983 voting rights in the denominator` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the voting rights held` TIMES 10 AT LEAST holdings's `s 983 voting rights in the denominator` TIMES 9))
    WHERE
        `the value held` MEANS
              holdings's `s 983 value acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances`
            PLUS holdings's `s 983 value of other shares the offeror has acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire`
            PLUS (IF `conditional contracts are taken into account` THEN holdings's `s 983 value of other shares the offeror has contracted to acquire subject to conditions not yet met` ELSE 0)
            PLUS (IF `s 983(8) the shares count as shares the offeror has acquired or contracted to acquire` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN holdings's `s 983 value of shares an associate has acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire` ELSE 0)
            PLUS (IF `conditional contracts are taken into account` THEN holdings's `s 983 value of shares an associate has contracted to acquire subject to conditions not yet met` ELSE 0)
            PLUS (IF `s 983(5) the shares are treated as having been acquired by the offeror` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN holdings's `s 983 value of shares held by the company as treasury shares` ELSE 0)
        `the voting rights held` MEANS
              holdings's `s 983 voting rights carried by the shares acquired by virtue of acceptances`
            PLUS holdings's `s 983 voting rights carried by those other shares`
            PLUS (IF `conditional contracts are taken into account` THEN holdings's `s 983 voting rights carried by those conditionally contracted shares` ELSE 0)
            PLUS holdings's `s 983 voting rights carried by those shares of an associate`
            PLUS (IF `conditional contracts are taken into account` THEN holdings's `s 983 voting rights carried by those conditionally contracted shares of an associate` ELSE 0)

-- s 983(1): subsections (2) and (3) apply where the takeover offer relates to all the shares in the company (the meaning of section 974).
-- src:13717 | (1) Subsections (2) and (3) apply in a case where a takeover offer relates to all the shares in a company.
-- src:13718 | For this purpose a takeover offer relates to all the shares in a company if it is an offer to acquire all the shares in the company within the meaning of section 974.
@ref s 983(1) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13717-13718)
GIVEN `the takeover offer is an offer to acquire all the shares in the company within the meaning of section 974` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` MEANS
    IF `the takeover offer is an offer to acquire all the shares in the company within the meaning of section 974`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) and (3) apply in a case where a takeover offer relates to all the shares in a company."

-- s 983(2): the holder of voting shares who has not accepted may require the offeror to acquire them if, before the end of the acceptance period, the offeror holds some but not all, and the holdings reach 90%.
-- src:13719 | (2) The holder of any voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13720 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13721 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares in the company which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)—
-- src:13722 | (i) amount to not less than 90% in value of all the voting shares in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)), and
-- src:13723 | (ii) carry not less than 90% of the voting rights in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)).
@ref s 983(2) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13719-13723)
GIVEN `s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the holder has not accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has by virtue of acceptances acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
      `the holdings, counting debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` IS A `s 983 holdings`
      `the holdings, leaving out debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` IS A `s 983 holdings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(2) the holder of voting shares may require the offeror to acquire them` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) and (3) apply in a case where a takeover offer relates to all the shares in a company."
    ELSE IF NOT (`the holder has not accepted the offer`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is of "The holder of any voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer"
         ELSE IF       `the day` AT MOST `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted`
                   AND `the offeror has by virtue of acceptances acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates`
                   AND (   `s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` `the holdings, counting debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` TRUE TRUE
                        OR `s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` `the holdings, leaving out debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` TRUE TRUE)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given "if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted" the offeror has acquired some (but not all) of the shares and the holdings reach 90%, and the text does not say "may not" (fork F16)

-- s 983(3): the holder of non-voting shares who has not accepted may require the offeror to acquire them if the holdings reach 90% in value of all the shares in the company.
-- src:13724 | (3) The holder of any non-voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13725 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13726 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares in the company which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met), amount to not less than 90% in value of all the shares in the company (or would do so but for section 990(1)).
@ref s 983(3) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13724-13726)
GIVEN `s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the holder has not accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has by virtue of acceptances acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
      `the holdings, counting debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` IS A `s 983 holdings`
      `the holdings, leaving out debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` IS A `s 983 holdings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(3) the holder of non-voting shares may require the offeror to acquire them` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) and (3) apply in a case where a takeover offer relates to all the shares in a company."
    ELSE IF NOT (`the holder has not accepted the offer`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is of "The holder of any non-voting shares to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer"
         ELSE IF       `the day` AT MOST `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted`
                   AND `the offeror has by virtue of acceptances acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares to which the offer relates`
                   AND (   `s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` `the holdings, counting debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` TRUE FALSE
                        OR `s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` `the holdings, leaving out debentures treated as shares by section 990(1)` TRUE FALSE)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given "if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted" the offeror has acquired some (but not all) of the shares and the holdings reach 90%, and the text does not say "may not" (fork F17)

-- s 983(4): where the offer relates to shares of one or more classes, the holder of shares of a class may require the offeror to acquire them if the holdings of that class reach 90%.
-- src:13727 | (4) If a takeover offer relates to shares of one or more classes and at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted—
-- src:13728 | (a) the offeror has by virtue of acceptances of the offer acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares of any class to which the offer relates, and
-- src:13729 | (b) those shares, with or without any other shares of that class which he has acquired or contracted to acquire (whether unconditionally or subject to conditions being met)—
-- src:13730 | (i) amount to not less than 90% in value of all the shares of that class, and
-- src:13731 | (ii) in a case where the shares of that class are voting shares, carry not less than 90% of the voting rights carried by the shares of that class,
-- src:13732 | the holder of any shares of that class to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer may require the offeror to acquire those shares.
@ref s 983(4) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13727-13732)
GIVEN `the holder has not accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has by virtue of acceptances acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares of the class to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
      `the holdings of the class` IS A `s 983 holdings`
      `the shares of that class are voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(4) the holder of shares of the class may require the offeror to acquire them` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the holder has not accepted the offer`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is of "the holder of any shares of that class to which the offer relates who has not accepted the offer"
    ELSE IF       `the day` AT MOST `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted`
              AND `the offeror has by virtue of acceptances acquired or unconditionally contracted to acquire some (but not all) of the shares of the class to which the offer relates`
              AND `s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` `the holdings of the class` TRUE `the shares of that class are voting shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given "if, at any time before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted" the offeror has acquired some (but not all) of the shares and the holdings reach 90%, and the text does not say "may not" (fork F18)

-- s 983(6): subsection (7) applies where a shareholder exercises his rights while shares are contracted for subject to conditions and the requirement would not be met without them.
-- src:13734 | (6) Subsection (7) applies where—
-- src:13735 | (a) a shareholder exercises rights conferred on him by subsection (2), (3) or (4),
-- src:13736 | (b) at the time when he does so, there are shares in the company which the offeror has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and in relation to which the contract has not become unconditional, and
-- src:13737 | (c) the requirement imposed by subsection (2)(b), (3)(b) or (4)(b) (as the case may be) would not be satisfied if those shares were not taken into account.
@ref s 983(6) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13734-13737)
GIVEN `a shareholder exercises rights conferred on him by subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are shares in the company which the offeror has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and the contract has not become unconditional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement in subsection (2)(b), (3)(b) or (4)(b) would not be satisfied if those shares were not taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(6) subsection (7) applies` MEANS
    IF `a shareholder exercises rights conferred on him by subsection (2), (3) or (4)` AND `there are shares in the company which the offeror has contracted to acquire subject to conditions being met, and the contract has not become unconditional` AND `the requirement in subsection (2)(b), (3)(b) or (4)(b) would not be satisfied if those shares were not taken into account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (7) applies where— (a) a shareholder exercises rights conferred on him by subsection (2), (3) or (4)"

-- s 983(7): the shareholder is treated, for section 985, as not having exercised his rights unless the requirement would be satisfied counting only unconditional contracts and the period in section 984(2).
-- src:13738 | (7) The shareholder is treated for the purposes of section 985 as not having exercised his rights under this section unless the requirement imposed by paragraph (b) of subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) would be satisfied if—
-- src:13739 | (a) the reference in that paragraph to other shares in the company which the offeror has contracted to acquire unconditionally or subject to conditions being met were a reference to such shares which he has unconditionally contracted to acquire, and
-- src:13740 | (b) the reference in that subsection to the period within which the offer can be accepted were a reference to the period referred to in section 984(2).
@ref s 983(7) Right of minority shareholder to be bought out by offeror (src:13738-13740)
GIVEN `s 983(6) subsection (7) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      holdings IS A `s 983 holdings`
      `the voting rights test applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the shareholder exercises the rights` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period referred to in section 984(2)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 983(7) the shareholder is treated as having exercised his rights for the purposes of section 985` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 983(6) subsection (7) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection "applies where" subsection (6) is met
    ELSE IF `s 983(2)(b) the holdings reach 90%` holdings FALSE `the voting rights test applies` AND `the day the shareholder exercises the rights` AT MOST `the last day of the period referred to in section 984(2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The shareholder is treated for the purposes of section 985 as not having exercised his rights under this section unless the requirement imposed by paragraph (b) of subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) would be satisfied if"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Further provision about the rights (ss 984 and 985)`

-- s 984(1): rights conferred by section 983 are exercisable by a written communication addressed to the offeror.
-- src:13743 | (1) Rights conferred on a shareholder by subsection (2), (3) or (4) of section 983 are exercisable by a written communication addressed to the offeror.
@ref s 984(1) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13743-13743)
GIVEN `the shareholder's communication is written and addressed to the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(1) the rights are exercised by the communication` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder's communication is written and addressed to the offeror`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rights "are exercisable by a written communication addressed to the offeror"

-- s 984(2): the rights are not exercisable after the end of three months from the later of the end of the acceptance period and the date of the notice to be given under (3).
-- src:13744 | (2) Rights conferred on a shareholder by subsection (2), (3) or (4) of that section are not exercisable after the end of the period of three months from—
-- src:13745 | (a) the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, or
-- src:13746 | (b) if later, the date of the notice that must be given under subsection (3) below.
@ref s 984(2) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13744-13746)
GIVEN `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
      `the date of the notice that must be given under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 984(2) the last day on which the rights may be exercised` MEANS
    `add months` `the later date` 3
    WHERE
        `the later date` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date of the notice that must be given under subsection (3)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted`
            WHEN JUST n THEN IF n GREATER THAN `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted` THEN n ELSE `the last day of the period within which the offer can be accepted`

-- src:13744 | (2) Rights conferred on a shareholder by subsection (2), (3) or (4) of that section are not exercisable after the end of the period of three months from—
-- src:13745 | (a) the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, or
-- src:13746 | (b) if later, the date of the notice that must be given under subsection (3) below.
@ref s 984(2) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13744-13746)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the rights may be exercised` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(2) the rights are exercisable on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT MOST `the last day on which the rights may be exercised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not exercisable after the end of the period of three months from"

-- s 984(3): within one month of the time specified in section 983(2), (3) or (4) the offeror must give the shareholder notice of the rights and the period (read: the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted; fork F6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:13747 | (3) Within one month of the time specified in subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) of that section, the offeror must give any shareholder who has not accepted the offer notice in the prescribed manner of—
-- src:13748 | (a) the rights that are exercisable by the shareholder under that subsection, and
-- src:13749 | (b) the period within which the rights are exercisable.
-- src:13750 | If the notice is given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, it must state that the offer is still open for acceptance.
@ref s 984(3) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13747-13750)
GIVEN `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 984(3) the last day for giving the notice` MEANS `add months` `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted` 1

-- src:13747 | (3) Within one month of the time specified in subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) of that section, the offeror must give any shareholder who has not accepted the offer notice in the prescribed manner of—
-- src:13748 | (a) the rights that are exercisable by the shareholder under that subsection, and
-- src:13749 | (b) the period within which the rights are exercisable.
-- src:13750 | If the notice is given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, it must state that the offer is still open for acceptance.
@ref s 984(3) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13747-13750)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(3) the notice was given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is given` AT MOST (`s 984(3) the last day for giving the notice` `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within one month of the time specified in subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) of that section, the offeror must give any shareholder who has not accepted the offer notice in the prescribed manner"

-- src:13747 | (3) Within one month of the time specified in subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) of that section, the offeror must give any shareholder who has not accepted the offer notice in the prescribed manner of—
-- src:13748 | (a) the rights that are exercisable by the shareholder under that subsection, and
-- src:13749 | (b) the period within which the rights are exercisable.
-- src:13750 | If the notice is given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, it must state that the offer is still open for acceptance.
@ref s 984(3) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13747-13750)
GIVEN `the notice was given in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the rights that are exercisable by the shareholder and the period within which they are exercisable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the offer is still open for acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(3) the notice has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice was given in the prescribed manner` AND `the notice states the rights that are exercisable by the shareholder and the period within which they are exercisable` AND ((NOT (`the notice was given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted`)) OR `the notice states that the offer is still open for acceptance`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the notice is given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, it must state that the offer is still open for acceptance."

-- s 984(3) as a regulative rule: the offeror must give notice within one month of the end of the acceptance period (the days allowed are counted from that date).
DECLARE `s 984 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 984 the offeror`

DECLARE `s 984 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 984(3) give the shareholder notice of his rights and the period`

-- src:13747 | (3) Within one month of the time specified in subsection (2), (3) or (4) (as the case may be) of that section, the offeror must give any shareholder who has not accepted the offer notice in the prescribed manner of—
-- src:13748 | (a) the rights that are exercisable by the shareholder under that subsection, and
-- src:13749 | (b) the period within which the rights are exercisable.
-- src:13750 | If the notice is given before the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted, it must state that the offer is still open for acceptance.
@ref s 984(3) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13747-13750)
GIVEN `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 984 party` `s 984 act`
`s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 984 the offeror`
    MUST `s 984(3) give the shareholder notice of his rights and the period`
    WITHIN ((Day (`s 984(3) the last day for giving the notice` `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted`)) MINUS (Day `the end of the period within which the offer can be accepted`))
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 984 the offeror` BECAUSE "the notice of the shareholder's rights was not given within one month of the end of the period within which the offer could be accepted"

-- s 984(4): subsection (3) does not apply if the offeror has given the shareholder a notice in respect of the shares under section 979.
-- src:13751 | (4) Subsection (3) does not apply if the offeror has given the shareholder a notice in respect of the shares in question under section 979.
@ref s 984(4) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13751-13751)
GIVEN `the offeror has given the shareholder a notice in respect of the shares in question under section 979` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(4) subsection (3) applies` MEANS
    IF `the offeror has given the shareholder a notice in respect of the shares in question under section 979`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) does not apply if the offeror has given the shareholder a notice in respect of the shares in question under section 979."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says when subsection (3) does not apply, not when it does

-- s 984(5): an offeror who fails to comply with (3) commits an offence; if a company, every officer in default or to whose neglect the failure is attributable also commits one.
DECLARE `s 984(5) who` IS ONE OF
    `s 984(5) the offeror`
    `s 984(5) an officer of the offeror company`

-- src:13752 | (5) An offeror who fails to comply with subsection (3) commits an offence.
-- src:13753 | If the offeror is a company, every officer of that company who is in default or to whose neglect the failure is attributable also commits an offence.
@ref s 984(5) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13752-13753)
GIVEN `the offeror fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      who IS A `s 984(5) who`
      `the offeror is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the failure is attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offeror fails to comply with subsection (3)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "An offeror who fails to comply with subsection (3)"
    ELSE CONSIDER who
         WHEN `s 984(5) the offeror` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 984(5) an officer of the offeror company` THEN
             IF NOT (`the offeror is a company`)
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the offeror is a company, every officer of that company"
             ELSE IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the failure is attributable to the officer's neglect`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the officer must be "in default or to whose neglect the failure is attributable"

-- s 984(6): if an offeror other than a company is charged, it is a defence for him to prove he took all reasonable steps.
-- src:13754 | (6) If an offeror other than a company is charged with an offence for failing to comply with subsection (3), it is a defence for him to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that subsection.
@ref s 984(6) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13754-13754)
GIVEN `the offeror is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror proves that he took all reasonable steps for securing compliance with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 984(6) the section gives the offeror a defence` MEANS
    IF `the offeror is a company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the defence is for "an offeror other than a company"
    ELSE IF `the offeror proves that he took all reasonable steps for securing compliance with subsection (3)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offeror other than a company is charged with an offence for failing to comply with subsection (3), it is a defence for him to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that subsection."
    -- this section gives no defence on these facts (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); that is not to say the person has no defence at all

-- s 984(7): the penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and a daily default fine of one-fiftieth of the statutory maximum (or, on the substituted words, of the greater of 5,000 pounds or level 4).
-- src:13755 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:13756 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:13757 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fiftieth of the statutory maximumone-fiftieth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences.
@ref s 984(7) Further provision about rights conferred by section 983 (src:13755-13757)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the substituted words apply (the greater of 5,000 pounds or the level 4 amount)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 980(8) penalty`
`s 984(7) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (`s 980(8) penalty` OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (`s 980(8) penalty` OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST `the daily fine`, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (`s 980(8) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST `the daily fine`, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (`s 980(8) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST `the daily fine`, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (`s 980(8) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST `the daily fine`, FALSE)
    WHERE
        `the daily fine` MEANS
            IF `the substituted words apply (the greater of 5,000 pounds or the level 4 amount)`
            THEN `s 980(8) a fraction of the greater of an amount in pounds and a level on the standard scale for summary offences` 0.02 5000 4
            ELSE `s 980(8) a fraction of the statutory maximum` 0.02

-- s 985(2): the offeror is entitled and bound to acquire the shares on the terms of the offer or on such other terms as may be agreed (subject to section 986).
-- src:13760 | (2) The offeror is entitled and bound to acquire those shares on the terms of the offer or on such other terms as may be agreed.
@ref s 985(2) Effect of requirement under section 983 (src:13760-13760)
GIVEN `the shareholder exercises his rights under section 983 in respect of shares held by him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 986 the court has made an order about the terms` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 985(2) the offeror is entitled and bound to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the shareholder exercises his rights under section 983 in respect of shares held by him`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section "applies where a shareholder exercises his rights under section 983"
    ELSE IF `s 986 the court has made an order about the terms` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is "Subject to section 986", whose order governs
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- on the terms of the offer or on such other terms as may be agreed

-- s 985(3): where the terms give a choice of consideration the shareholder may indicate his choice when requiring the offeror to acquire, and the notice under section 984(3) must give particulars and may state the default.
-- src:13761 | (3) Where the terms of an offer are such as to give the shareholder a choice of consideration—
-- src:13762 | (a) the shareholder may indicate his choice when requiring the offeror to acquire the shares, and
-- src:13763 | (b) the notice given to the shareholder under section 984(3)—
-- src:13764 | (i) must give particulars of the choice and of the rights conferred by this subsection, and
-- src:13765 | (ii) may state which consideration specified in the offer will apply if he does not indicate a choice.
-- src:13766 | The reference in subsection (2) to the terms of the offer is to be read accordingly.
@ref s 985(3) Effect of requirement under section 983 (src:13761-13766)
GIVEN `the terms of the offer give the shareholder a choice of consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 985(3)(a) the shareholder may indicate his choice when requiring the offeror to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF `the terms of the offer give the shareholder a choice of consideration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for terms "such as to give the shareholder a choice of consideration"

-- src:13761 | (3) Where the terms of an offer are such as to give the shareholder a choice of consideration—
-- src:13762 | (a) the shareholder may indicate his choice when requiring the offeror to acquire the shares, and
-- src:13763 | (b) the notice given to the shareholder under section 984(3)—
-- src:13764 | (i) must give particulars of the choice and of the rights conferred by this subsection, and
-- src:13765 | (ii) may state which consideration specified in the offer will apply if he does not indicate a choice.
-- src:13766 | The reference in subsection (2) to the terms of the offer is to be read accordingly.
@ref s 985(3) Effect of requirement under section 983 (src:13761-13766)
GIVEN `the terms of the offer give the shareholder a choice of consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice under section 984(3) gives particulars of the choice and of the rights conferred by this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 985(3)(b) the notice under section 984(3) is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the terms of the offer give the shareholder a choice of consideration`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for terms "such as to give the shareholder a choice of consideration"
    ELSE IF `the notice under section 984(3) gives particulars of the choice and of the rights conferred by this subsection`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- the notice may also state which consideration applies if he does not indicate a choice
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice given to the shareholder under section 984(3)— (i) must give particulars of the choice and of the rights conferred by this subsection"

-- s 985(4): subsection (3) applies whether or not any time-limit or other conditions applicable to the choice can still be complied with.
-- src:13767 | (4) Subsection (3) applies whether or not any time-limit or other conditions applicable to the choice under the terms of the offer can still be complied with.
@ref s 985(4) Effect of requirement under section 983 (src:13767-13767)
GIVEN `a time-limit or other condition applicable to the choice under the terms of the offer can still be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 985(4) subsection (3) applies` MEANS
    IF `a time-limit or other condition applicable to the choice under the terms of the offer can still be complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- the subsection applies in either case: "whether or not"

-- s 985(5): where the consideration cannot be provided it is the cash equivalent at the date the shareholder requires the offeror to acquire the shares.
-- src:13768 | (5) If the consideration offered to or (as the case may be) chosen by the shareholder—
-- src:13769 | (a) is not cash and the offeror is no longer able to provide it, or
-- src:13770 | (b) was to have been provided by a third party who is no longer bound or able to provide it,
-- src:13771 | the consideration is to be taken to consist of an amount of cash, payable by the offeror, which at the date when the shareholder requires the offeror to acquire the shares is equivalent to the consideration offered or (as the case may be) chosen.
@ref s 985(5) Effect of requirement under section 983 (src:13768-13771)
GIVEN `the consideration offered or chosen is not cash and the offeror is no longer able to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration was to have been provided by a third party who is no longer bound or able to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cash amount equivalent to the consideration at the date the shareholder requires the offeror to acquire the shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 985(5) the cash consideration the offeror must pay` MEANS
    IF `the consideration offered or chosen is not cash and the offeror is no longer able to provide it` OR `the consideration was to have been provided by a third party who is no longer bound or able to provide it`
    THEN JUST `the cash amount equivalent to the consideration at the date the shareholder requires the offeror to acquire the shares`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the cash equivalent applies only if the consideration is "not cash and the offeror is no longer able to provide it" or "was to have been provided by a third party who is no longer bound or able to provide it"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Applications to the court (s 986)`

-- s 986(1): where a notice is given under section 979 to a shareholder the court may, on his application, order that the offeror is not entitled and bound to acquire, or that the terms are as the court thinks fit.
-- src:13774 | (1) Where a notice is given under section 979 to a shareholder the court may, on an application made by him, order—
-- src:13775 | (a) that the offeror is not entitled and bound to acquire the shares to which the notice relates, or
-- src:13776 | (b) that the terms on which the offeror is entitled and bound to acquire the shares shall be such as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 986(1) Applications to the court (src:13774-13776)
GIVEN `a notice is given under section 979 to the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(1) the court may make an order on the shareholder's application` MEANS
    IF `a notice is given under section 979 to the shareholder` AND `the application is made by the shareholder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "Where a notice is given under section 979 to a shareholder", "on an application made by him"

-- s 986(2): the application must be made within six weeks from the date on which the notice was given; if pending at the end of that period, section 981(6) does not have effect until it is disposed of.
-- src:13777 | (2) An application under subsection (1) must be made within six weeks from the date on which the notice referred to in that subsection was given.
-- src:13778 | If an application to the court under subsection (1) is pending at the end of that period, section 981(6) does not have effect until the application has been disposed of.
@ref s 986(2) Applications to the court (src:13777-13778)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 986(2) the last day for the application` MEANS `the date on which the notice was given` PLUS 42

-- src:13777 | (2) An application under subsection (1) must be made within six weeks from the date on which the notice referred to in that subsection was given.
-- src:13778 | If an application to the court under subsection (1) is pending at the end of that period, section 981(6) does not have effect until the application has been disposed of.
@ref s 986(2) Applications to the court (src:13777-13778)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(2) the application is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the application is made` AT MOST (`s 986(2) the last day for the application` `the date on which the notice was given`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (1) must be made within six weeks from the date on which the notice referred to in that subsection was given."

-- src:13777 | (2) An application under subsection (1) must be made within six weeks from the date on which the notice referred to in that subsection was given.
-- src:13778 | If an application to the court under subsection (1) is pending at the end of that period, section 981(6) does not have effect until the application has been disposed of.
@ref s 986(2) Applications to the court (src:13777-13778)
GIVEN `an application to the court under subsection (1) is pending at the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(2) section 981(6) has effect` MEANS
    IF `an application to the court under subsection (1) is pending at the end of that period`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application to the court under subsection (1) is pending at the end of that period, section 981(6) does not have effect until the application has been disposed of."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the suspension is of section 981(6) while an application "is pending at the end of that period"

-- s 986(3): where a shareholder exercises his rights under section 983 the court may, on the application of the shareholder or the offeror, order that the terms are as the court thinks fit.
-- src:13779 | (3) Where a shareholder exercises his rights under section 983 in respect of any shares held by him, the court may, on an application made by him or the offeror, order that the terms on which the offeror is entitled and bound to acquire the shares shall be such as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 986(3) Applications to the court (src:13779-13779)
GIVEN `the shareholder exercises his rights under section 983 in respect of shares held by him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the shareholder or the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(3) the court may order the terms on which the offeror is entitled and bound to acquire the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder exercises his rights under section 983 in respect of shares held by him` AND `the application is made by the shareholder or the offeror`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "Where a shareholder exercises his rights under section 983", "on an application made by him or the offeror"

-- s 986(4): on an application the court may not require consideration of a higher value than the offer value unless the holder shows the offer value would be unfair, nor a lower value.
-- src:13780 | (4) On an application under subsection (1) or (3)—
-- src:13781 | (a) the court may not require consideration of a higher value than that specified in the terms of the offer (“the offer value”) to be given for the shares to which the application relates unless the holder of the shares shows that the offer value would be unfair;
-- src:13782 | (b) the court may not require consideration of a lower value than the offer value to be given for the shares.
@ref s 986(4) Applications to the court (src:13780-13782)
GIVEN `the value of the consideration the court is asked to require` IS A NUMBER
      `the value specified in the terms of the offer (the offer value)` IS A NUMBER
      `the holder of the shares shows that the offer value would be unfair` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(4) the court may require consideration of that value` MEANS
    IF `the value of the consideration the court is asked to require` LESS THAN `the value specified in the terms of the offer (the offer value)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may not require consideration of a lower value than the offer value to be given for the shares"
    ELSE IF `the value of the consideration the court is asked to require` GREATER THAN `the value specified in the terms of the offer (the offer value)`
         THEN IF `the holder of the shares shows that the offer value would be unfair`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar on a higher value applies "unless the holder of the shares shows that the offer value would be unfair", and the text does not grant the power when the bar lifts
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may not require consideration of a higher value than that specified in the terms of the offer (“the offer value”) to be given for the shares to which the application relates unless the holder of the shares shows that the offer value would be unfair"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither bar speaks of a value equal to the offer value

-- s 986(5): no order for costs may be made against a shareholder making an application unless the court considers the application unnecessary, improper or vexatious, there was unreasonable delay, or unreasonable conduct.
-- src:13783 | (5) No order for costs or expenses may be made against a shareholder making an application under subsection (1) or (3) unless the court considers that—
-- src:13784 | (a) the application was unnecessary, improper or vexatious,
-- src:13785 | (b) there has been unreasonable delay in making the application, or
-- src:13786 | (c) there has been unreasonable conduct on the shareholder's part in conducting the proceedings on the application.
@ref s 986(5) Applications to the court (src:13783-13786)
GIVEN `the order is against a shareholder making an application under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that the application was unnecessary, improper or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that there has been unreasonable delay in making the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that there has been unreasonable conduct on the shareholder's part in conducting the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(5) an order for costs or expenses may be made against the shareholder` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the order is against a shareholder making an application under subsection (1) or (3)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on an order "against a shareholder making an application under subsection (1) or (3)"
    ELSE IF `the court considers that the application was unnecessary, improper or vexatious` OR `the court considers that there has been unreasonable delay in making the application` OR `the court considers that there has been unreasonable conduct on the shareholder's part in conducting the proceedings`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar lifts "unless the court considers that" one of (a) to (c) is met, and the text does not itself grant the power
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order for costs or expenses may be made against a shareholder making an application under subsection (1) or (3) unless the court considers that"

-- s 986(6): a shareholder who has made an application must give notice of it to the offeror.
-- src:13787 | (6) A shareholder who has made an application under subsection (1) or (3) must give notice of the application to the offeror.
@ref s 986(6) Applications to the court (src:13787-13787)
GIVEN `the shareholder gave notice of the application to the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(6) the shareholder has given the offeror notice of the application` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder gave notice of the application to the offeror`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A shareholder who has made an application under subsection (1) or (3) must give notice of the application to the offeror."

-- s 986(7): an offeror given notice of an application must give a copy to (a) any other person given a notice under section 979, (b) any person who has exercised his rights under section 983.
DECLARE `s 986(7) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 986(7)(a) a person other than the applicant to whom a notice has been given under section 979`
    `s 986(7) the applicant`
    `s 986(7)(b) a person who has exercised his rights under section 983`
    `s 986(7) another person`

-- src:13788 | (7) An offeror who is given notice of an application under subsection (1) or (3) must give a copy of the notice to—
-- src:13789 | (a) any person (other than the applicant) to whom a notice has been given under section 979;
-- src:13790 | (b) any person who has exercised his rights under section 983.
@ref s 986(7) Applications to the court (src:13788-13790)
GIVEN person IS A `s 986(7) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(7) the offeror must give the person a copy of the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `s 986(7)(a) a person other than the applicant to whom a notice has been given under section 979` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 986(7) the applicant` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any person (other than the applicant) to whom a notice has been given under section 979"
    WHEN `s 986(7)(b) a person who has exercised his rights under section 983` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 986(7) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to the two kinds of person listed

-- s 986(8): an offeror who applies under subsection (3) must give notice of the application to (a) any person to whom a notice has been given under section 979, (b) any person who has exercised his rights under section 983.
DECLARE `s 986(8) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 986(8)(a) a person to whom a notice has been given under section 979`
    `s 986(8)(b) a person who has exercised his rights under section 983`
    `s 986(8) another person`

-- src:13791 | (8) An offeror who makes an application under subsection (3) must give notice of the application to—
-- src:13792 | (a) any person to whom a notice has been given under section 979;
-- src:13793 | (b) any person who has exercised his rights under section 983.
@ref s 986(8) Applications to the court (src:13791-13793)
GIVEN person IS A `s 986(8) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(8) the offeror must give the person notice of the application` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `s 986(8)(a) a person to whom a notice has been given under section 979` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 986(8)(b) a person who has exercised his rights under section 983` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 986(8) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to the two kinds of person listed

-- s 986(9) and (10): the court may authorise the offeror to give notices where the offer has not been accepted to the necessary extent, if (a) to (c) are met and it is just and equitable.
-- src:13794 | (9) Where a takeover offer has not been accepted to the extent necessary for entitling the offeror to give notices under subsection (2) or (4) of section 979 the court may, on an application made by him, make an order authorising him to give notices under that subsection if it is satisfied that—
-- src:13795 | (a) the offeror has after reasonable enquiry been unable to trace one or more of the persons holding shares to which the offer relates,
-- src:13796 | (b) the requirements of that subsection would have been met if the person, or all the persons, mentioned in paragraph (a) above had accepted the offer, and
-- src:13797 | (c) the consideration offered is fair and reasonable.
-- src:13798 | This is subject to subsection (10).
-- src:13799 | (10) The court may not make an order under subsection (9) unless it considers that it is just and equitable to do so having regard, in particular, to the number of shareholders who have been traced but who have not accepted the offer.
@ref s 986(9)-(10) Order authorising the offeror to give notices (src:13794-13799)
GIVEN `the takeover offer has not been accepted to the extent necessary for entitling the offeror to give notices under subsection (2) or (4) of section 979` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has after reasonable enquiry been unable to trace one or more of the persons holding shares to which the offer relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of that subsection would have been met if the person, or all the persons, mentioned in paragraph (a) had accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration offered is fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that it is just and equitable to make the order, having regard in particular to the number of shareholders who have been traced but who have not accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 986(9) the court may authorise the offeror to give notices under section 979` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the takeover offer has not been accepted to the extent necessary for entitling the offeror to give notices under subsection (2) or (4) of section 979`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "Where a takeover offer has not been accepted to the extent necessary for entitling the offeror to give notices under subsection (2) or (4) of section 979"
    ELSE IF `the offeror has after reasonable enquiry been unable to trace one or more of the persons holding shares to which the offer relates` AND `the requirements of that subsection would have been met if the person, or all the persons, mentioned in paragraph (a) had accepted the offer` AND `the consideration offered is fair and reasonable`
         THEN IF `the court considers that it is just and equitable to make the order, having regard in particular to the number of shareholders who have been traced but who have not accepted the offer`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may not make an order under subsection (9) unless it considers that it is just and equitable to do so"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court may make the order "if it is satisfied that" (a) the offeror has after reasonable enquiry been unable to trace one or more of the holders, (b) the requirements would have been met had they accepted, and (c) the consideration is fair and reasonable, and the text does not say "may not" (fork F19); the bar in subsection (10) is a "may not ... unless" and keeps JUST FALSE
